 package — a root `__init__.py` with the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports plus 29 submodules moved by rope under the AST body oracle (bead forge-plugin-2fc, plan `.refactor/plan-engine.md`). Two non-move edits ride with it: the merge bootstrap child resolves `scripts/forge/cli.py` from `runtime.py`'s location instead of its own file depth (E1, with a focused test), and tests patch engine controls through one `patch_engine` loader helper (E0; the hermetic chain fixture assigns the codex executable on every engine module that binds it). The reviewer-facing eval trigger table names `scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/**` in place of `engine.py` in the spec, the policy constant, the rendered project files and the fixtures; the Revision-9 seam-marker loop moves from the `chain_core` package root to `_commit_chain.py` beside `register_coordination_seams` (bead forge-plugin-4j7, finding CON-02; its grandfathered size entry rises 1840 -> 1847 by operator direction of 2026-09-17); the FR-230 production subjects are the engine package files, re-minted; the size baseline is re-pinned at measured sizes (`engine/_engine.py`, the `Engine` class, is the one new over-budget entry), the ruff per-file ignores are narrowed per engine module, and an import-linter layers contract locks the package's wave order.\n - Test isolation (beads forge-plugin-0eq, forge-plugin-ehn): `tests/test_audit_commitments.py` writes its disabled-control mutants of `audit-commitments.py` under a private temp directory (pinning the script's plugin root) instead of beside the real script, so a parallel Gate 1 shard copying the tracked `scripts/` tree no longer races on a vanishing sibling; `tests/test_mutation_runner.py` sets `FORGE_SESSION_PID` to the test process for the runner child instead of inheriting the caller's value, so an exported session identity no longer fails ten tests with a foreign-live-owner refusal.\n - chain_core split follow-ups (bead forge-plugin-r0b; review-final findings at reintegration): `scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/_state.py` declares its constants in the historical module order again (bodies unchanged; FR-230 manifest, result fixtures and the v2 byte pin re-minted for the changed production subject); the spec's package sentence names the submodules by the FR-230 manifest's production-subject list instead of the planning document; `pyproject.toml` per-file-ignores drop the dead `chain_core.py` entry and the blanket `chain_core/**` glob in favour of one entry per submodule listing only the codes it trips, and `scripts/check_file_length.py` is cleaned to the full rule set (its entry removed) and gains a focused unittest (`tests/test_check_file_length.py`: hook and plain-mode exit codes, the exact guard diagnostic, and an in-memory control-disable leg); `import-linter==2.15` is pinned beside ruff in the guardrails workflow and the pre-commit setup line. Disclosure: the 0.6.12 reintegration's `.claude/settings.json` also carries `worktree.baseRef: head` and `enabledPlugins: codex-orchestrator@codex-orchestrator` (operator-approved at Gate 4 on 2026-09-14; the plugin entry dangles on a clone without that marketplace). Deferred to the `_commit_chain` split (bead forge-plugin-4j7): moving the Revision-9 seam-marker loop out of the package root, because the grandfathered `_commit_chain.py` may not grow.\ndiff --git a/docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md b/docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md\nindex 59298de..c93ea64 100644\n--- a/docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md\n+++ b/docs/specs/forge-plugin-spec.md\n@@ -114,7 +114,7 @@ leaves the commit untouched, records a failed identity verification, and freezes\n - `agents/review-final.md` — instruction-bounded, execution-capable Claude reviewer with a binding verdict; it has no Edit/Write tools but shares the orchestrator's writable worktree, so its no-write boundary is not an OS sandbox\n - `scripts/forge/{check-halt.sh,acquire-commit-lock.sh,release-commit-lock.sh,run-evals.sh,invariant-guard.sh,configure-dcg.sh,drift-check.sh,drift-staleness.sh,aggregate-telemetry.sh,commit-guard.sh,install.sh}` and `scripts/forge/{check-test-quality.py,archive-run.py,audit-commitments.py,emit-decision-event.py,journal-patterns.py}` — executable governance script surfaces\n - `scripts/forge/run-scoped-mutation.py` — Python-interpreter-loaded governance helper (the merge path invokes it as `python3 <path>` and the drift path imports it), so it is outside the executable-script inventory\n-- `scripts/forge/forge_cli/` — the Python-interpreter-loaded package the Forge CLI is being split into (bead forge-plugin-95e): `scripts/forge/cli.py` remains the sole invoked entry point and shim that FR-221's matcher and the FR-223 corpora pin; the shim puts its own directory on `sys.path`, re-imports the envelope and policy names by explicit named lists, and forwards attribute reads of every `runtime`, `chain_core`, `engine`, and `app` `__all__` export through a module `__getattr__` (PEP 562), so every historical module attribute stays resolvable while tests reach the package through one shared loader (`tests/_cli_loader.py`); no file under it is executable, and it is outside the executable-script inventory exactly as `run-scoped-mutation.py` is. The package holds `envelope.py` (reason codes, `Refusal`, `FrozenError`, `Outcome`), `policy.py` (the committed-policy parser, whose fence helpers are the canonical patch seams), `runtime.py` (the one canonical module for the patchable controls — the clock, the bounded process runner, the merge lifecycle flag, the Revision-9 state controls, the path roots, the lazily imported coordination modules, the fast-tier mechanical-skip predicate, and the late-bound journal-record builder seam — which every module of the split reads by attribute so one in-memory patch on `forge_cli.runtime` disables a control everywhere), `candidate.py` (the shared bounded, pinned Git-context implementation for immutable tree snapshots, deterministic review evidence, marker identity, and raw produced-commit inspection), the `chain_core/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the historical module defined (its unused imports are not re-bound on the root), and whose modules — the root `__init__.py` and the submodules, together exactly the `scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/` production subjects listed in `.forge/evals/tasks/fr230-phase3-4-v2.manifest.json` — hold the fenced process runner, the FR-235 common-lock arbiter and chain leases, chain and merge-chain storage, merge state and transition validation, the ingest verifiers, and the Revision-9 seam-marker loop (in `_commit_chain.py` beside `register_coordination_seams`, with `_seam` re-exported on the root for attribute parity)), the `engine/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the historical `engine.py` defined (names it merely imported are re-bound on the root only where an importer or test reads them there), and whose submodules — the root and the submodules together exactly the `scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/` production subjects listed in `.forge/evals/tasks/fr230-phase3-4-v2.manifest.json` — hold the `Engine` commit-chain class (`_engine.py`), argument-parser construction, the finalize pipeline, review transport, approval, secret-scan and fresh-eval helpers, the archive surface, merge admission/scope/claim/epoch/conflict/worktree helpers, and the Revision-12 bootstrap child protocol; `_journal.py` binds the journal-record builder onto the runtime seam at import, and the bootstrap child re-execs `scripts/forge/cli.py` resolved from `runtime.py`'s own location), and `app.py` (`MergeEngine`, the shared chain-verb router, argument-parsing and dispatch entry points, and `main`; it obtains the parser and other engine helpers through `forge_cli.engine`). The existing FR-230 phase-3/4 manifest retains its historical production subjects; every changed or added production subject, including `candidate.py`, requires a current applicable Recorded-baseline integrity (`strict-evals`) result binding, plus `fresh-reviewer-evals` when the authenticated-base trigger matches; an unverifiable trigger blocks through its required INVALID path. The split changes no verb, diagnostic, reason code, `--help` byte, or immutable prior corpus.\n+- `scripts/forge/forge_cli/` — the Python-interpreter-loaded package the Forge CLI is being split into (bead forge-plugin-95e): `scripts/forge/cli.py` remains the sole invoked entry point and shim that FR-221's matcher and the FR-223 corpora pin; the shim puts its own directory on `sys.path`, re-imports the envelope and policy names by explicit named lists, and forwards attribute reads of every `runtime`, `chain_core`, `engine`, and `app` `__all__` export through a module `__getattr__` (PEP 562), so every historical module attribute stays resolvable while tests reach the package through one shared loader (`tests/_cli_loader.py`); no file under it is executable, and it is outside the executable-script inventory exactly as `run-scoped-mutation.py` is. The package holds `envelope.py` (reason codes, `Refusal`, `FrozenError`, `Outcome`), `policy.py` (the committed-policy parser, whose fence helpers are the canonical patch seams), `runtime.py` (the one canonical module for the patchable controls — the clock, the bounded process runner, the merge lifecycle flag, the Revision-9 state controls, the path roots, the lazily imported coordination modules, the fast-tier mechanical-skip predicate, and the late-bound journal-record builder seam — which every module of the split reads by attribute so one in-memory patch on `forge_cli.runtime` disables a control everywhere), `candidate.py` (the shared bounded, pinned Git-context implementation for immutable tree snapshots, deterministic review evidence, marker identity, and raw produced-commit inspection), the `chain_core/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the historical module defined (its unused imports are not re-bound on the root), and whose modules — the root `__init__.py` and the submodules, together exactly the `scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/` production subjects listed in `.forge/evals/tasks/fr230-phase3-4-v2.manifest.json` — hold the fenced process runner, the FR-235 common-lock arbiter and chain leases, chain and merge-chain storage, merge state and transition validation, the ingest verifiers, and the Revision-9 seam-marker loop (in `_commit_chain.py` beside `register_coordination_seams`, with `_seam` re-exported on the root for attribute parity)), the `engine/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the historical `engine.py` defined (names it merely imported are re-bound on the root only where an importer or test reads them there), and whose submodules — the root and the submodules together exactly the `scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/` production subjects listed in `.forge/evals/tasks/fr230-phase3-4-v2.manifest.json` — hold the `Engine` commit-chain class (`_engine.py`), argument-parser construction, the finalize pipeline, review transport, approval, secret-scan and fresh-eval helpers, the archive surface, merge admission/scope/claim/epoch/conflict/worktree helpers, and the Revision-12 bootstrap child protocol; `_journal.py` binds the journal-record builder onto the runtime seam at import, and the bootstrap child re-execs `scripts/forge/cli.py` resolved from `runtime.py`'s own location), and the `app/` package (`scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/`, whose root `__init__.py` holds the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the historical `app.py` defined, and whose modules — the root and the submodules together exactly the `scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/` production subjects listed in `.forge/evals/tasks/fr230-phase3-4-v2.manifest.json` — hold the `MergeEngine` merge-chain class (`_merge_engine.py`), merge-start admission (`_admission.py`), current-candidate observation (`_candidate_observation.py`), the deferred mutation-journal sideband helpers (`_mutation_journal.py`), and the shared chain-verb router, the dispatch entry point and `main` (`_dispatch.py`); it obtains the parser and other engine helpers through `forge_cli.engine`). The existing FR-230 phase-3/4 manifest retains its historical production subjects; every changed or added production subject, including `candidate.py`, requires a current applicable Recorded-baseline integrity (`strict-evals`) result binding, plus `fresh-reviewer-evals` when the authenticated-base trigger matches; an unverifiable trigger blocks through its required INVALID path. The split changes no verb, diagnostic, reason code, `--help` byte, or immutable prior corpus.\n - `scripts/forge/forge_cli/fresh_evals.py` — the non-executable, Python-interpreter-loaded internal collector and verifier for candidate-bound fresh reviewer evaluation; behind the chain-owned `engine/` package launcher adapter it implements authenticated trigger derivation, candidate-tree fixture inventory and oracle withholding, bounded native child execution, canonical request-bound artifacts, manifest verification, and the current-candidate PASS predicate without adding a second CLI entry point\n - `scripts/forge/cli.py` — the Forge CLI commit-chain slice (FR-210..FR-224): a persisted chain state machine invoked as `python3 \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/forge/cli.py\" <verb>`, owning commit-chain sequencing, staging, candidate identity, evidence capture, and finalize. No PATH binary named `forge` is installed (the Foundry `forge` collision); `forge <verb>` anywhere in this spec is shorthand for that invocation form. Phase-gated: ships only after the FR-223 precondition evals pass\n - Phase-3 Forge CLI merge surfaces specified by FR-230..FR-237: `status`, `merge start|refresh|verify|gate run|approve|finalize|recover|cleanup|abort`, and the shared `review request|attach|disposition` verbs. These are normative future surfaces, not implementation delivered by Revision 7.\ndiff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml\nindex e401919..1e6b59d 100644\n--- a/pyproject.toml\n+++ b/pyproject.toml\n@@ -57,7 +57,12 @@ max-nested-blocks = 4\n \"scripts/forge/cli.py\" = [\"F401\", \"I001\", \"UP035\"]\n \"scripts/forge/commitment_paths.py\" = [\"C901\", \"I001\", \"PLR0911\", \"PLR0912\"]\n \"scripts/forge/emit-decision-event.py\" = [\"C901\", \"I001\", \"PLR0911\", \"PLR0912\", \"PLR0915\", \"PLR1702\"]\n-\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app.py\" = [\"B023\", \"B904\", \"B905\", \"C901\", \"E501\", \"E731\", \"F401\", \"F811\", \"F841\", \"I001\", \"PLR0911\", \"PLR0912\", \"PLR0913\", \"PLR0915\", \"PLR1702\", \"UP012\", \"UP035\"]\n+\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/__init__.py\" = [\"I001\"]\n+\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/_admission.py\" = [\"C901\", \"I001\", \"PLR0912\", \"PLR0915\"]\n+\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/_candidate_observation.py\" = [\"C901\", \"I001\", \"PLR0912\", \"PLR0915\", \"UP035\"]\n+\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/_dispatch.py\" = [\"C901\", \"E501\", \"I001\", \"PLR0911\", \"PLR0912\", \"UP035\"]\n+\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/_merge_engine.py\" = [\"B023\", \"B904\", \"B905\", \"C901\", \"E501\", \"E731\", \"F841\", \"I001\", \"PLR0911\", \"PLR0912\", \"PLR0913\", \"PLR0915\", \"PLR1702\", \"UP012\", \"UP035\"]\n+\"scripts/forge/forge_cli/app/_mutation_journal.py\" = [\"C901\", \"I001\", \"UP035\"]\n \"scripts/forge/forge_cli/candidate.py\" = [\"B905\", \"C901\", \"E501\", \"I001\", \"PLR0911\", \"PLR0912\", \"PLR0913\", \"PLR0915\", \"PLR1702\", \"UP035\"]\n # chain_core/ package (split 2026-09-13; narrowed per module 2026-09-14, bead forge-plugin-r0b):\n # each entry lists only the codes that module trips, so the ratchet can tighten per file.\n@@ -304,6 +309,23 @@ ignore_imports = [\n     \"forge_cli.runtime ->